  "original_findings_text": "# B1 preparation attribution and one unprobed sampling run\n\nThe combined148-span prototype run ended0, both cases passed, all six source paths were restored exactly and saved geometry archives stayed unchanged. Its work941311 belongs to that prototype. The later perf run uses the independently preserved UNPROBED167-span executable, not that prototype. No source change, optimization or extra test execution occurred in this analysis.\n\n## Measured preparation:137-edge UV profile\n\n| Measurement | Inward | Outward |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Census checkpoint interval |5.694622095s|5.799079550s|\n| Census callbacks |2579676|2579676|\n| Actual delegated callback bodies |.064174713s|.064526960s|\n| Contact WorldConstruction interval/tail |1.506177930s|1.622495237s|\n| Cardinality total inside that tail |1.490458377s|1.606342420s|\n| Existing observed-row discovery |1.185206330s|1.282426512s|\n| Certificate binding within cardinality |.146174616s|.156647540s|\n\n9453reports were first visits, no visited hits; missed visited searches encountered44674878entries. Unique-vertex filtering was~.00028s. The callback body measurement excludes original caller-side polling machinery and does not authorize changing any poll. Intervals follow existing checkpoints; the WorldConstruction tail includes final admission. Nested numbers cannot be summed. Timer/aggregation and nested logging overhead remain; these are diagnostic timings.\n\nDirect lookup, metadata and owned source-recapture dominance are refuted. Current source freshness is6N as intended. A previous view profiler's~.9s metadata total is not the8s preparation cost. Seed duplication, local-walk and numeric-dependency hypotheses were separately rejected; do not revive them.\n\n## Authorized sampling: original167 executable\n\nOne command ran the exact outward test under the existing B1 qualification lock: perf record cycles:u99Hz, DWARF8192. Executable SHA61ed9ad5c70630c671ca930f52ce67d41bc513965e67b172d921285d3f9652a7 matches authoritative identity.json. Compiled source manifest1f90e3c0\u2026 matches current source at launch; source drift after run was empty. Historical build settings/profile provenance are retained in terminal.json. The test passed1/0, unchanged binary, arithmetic984593/cells501/spans167, diagnostic wall35.7929s; no matched timing claim under F1 load.\n\n3547samples,0lost.94.50% weighted cycles have zero/one recovered DWARF frame: inclusive caller attribution is unreliable. SELF samples: bigint division6.10%, bigint symbols~11.47%; std_detect3.01%; atomic functions~6.71%; contact topology~3.35%, notably matches_row1.93% and native_axis_parameters1.13%. These whole-operation self samples do NOT locate the bigint cost specifically inside Census. Reports/script/raw data and hashes are retained; no second run.\n\n## Smallest justified optimization seam (not implemented)\n\nObserved-row discovery is a measured1.2s target with direct sampled symbols. topology.rs:167 native_axis_parameters loops EVERY snapshot source, then matches_row:385 binary-searches SourceIndex membership for each. The index already exposes the exact matching source ROWS at source_index.rs:26. Its construction enumerates source rows in original order (:73), inserts candidates in that order (:96), and filtering (:102) preserves it.\n\nA conditioned Some(index) path could iterate those existing row positions directly and reuse append_source_parameters unchanged; the None path must keep its existing live predicate. Safe get must preserve malformed-index behavior. Preserve duplicate source rows, exact source_index values, parameter-bit dedup and first-encounter order. This removes repeated pure membership filtering without a new cache, geometry call or skipped cardinality check. Independent output/order/corrupt-index/refusal controls and measurement are still required before adoption. Its maximum measured scope is~1.2s, not a route alone to5s.\n\n## Census: next bounded discriminator and target implications\n\nCensus remains the largest identified non-native interval. Current data cannot separate Bernstein reuse search from exclusion arithmetic/fallback. The smallest next measurement is one operation-local enumeration aggregate separating EXISTING reuse lookup, capture, exclusion and inconclusive-only fallback calls/times; preserve callback/work/error order and emit once. Two source files suffice: paired_execution driver owns the aggregate and lends it to bernstein_execution's actual calls. No extra proofs, predicates or polls; no per-domain IO. This would refute either lookup or numerical work as dominant before changing Math. Sampling's bigint self cost supports investigating exact arithmetic, not a specific algebraic change.\n\nAn unchanged~17s native SI path already exceeds the5s end-to-end target. Removing~1.2s contact overhead or even all measured~5.8s Census cannot satisfy that target while preserving the rest unchanged. Significant further progress needs the separately owned rigorous SI/reference-body remediation and a measured general Census improvement; acceptance/coverage cannot be replaced by a fast sampled pass. #498 remains a separate proof obligation, and no new issue is filed from this analysis.\n",
